{
  "abstract": "For every natural N there is n at least N and an n-point set in the single fixed Euclidean space R^29 whose distances on different unordered pairs of distinct points differ by at least one, with diameter strictly below (499/500)n^2. The sizes n form an unbounded set; no claim is made for every large n. As a consequence the formalization proves the negation of the fixed-dimension proposition for Erdős Problem 670 exactly as stated in Formal Conjectures at commit 2f91d251c07fbbaf9435166d47c11e884a08a6cf, using d = 29 and epsilon = 1/1000. No optimality, smallest dimension or independent priority review is claimed.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "John Tripodo"
    }
  ],
